{"event":"step_update","step_update":{"conversation_id":"0bc9786a-969a-4dc5-8d7a-3d6f2fa267bb","step_index":66,"state":"DONE","step_type":"tool","tool_name":"run_command","duration_seconds":0.216730686,"tool_info":{"name":"run_command","parameters":{"CommandLine":"NO_COLOR=1 deno doc --unstable-kv packages/fresh/mod.ts | head -60"},"output":"`@netscript/fresh` provides Fresh runtime extensions, page builders, form primitives, and route contracts for NetScript.\r\n\r\nSubpath exports:\r\n\r\n- `.`: page-loader cache helpers and entry re-exports\r\n- `./builders`: type-safe page and layout definition wrappers\r\n- `./route`: route contracts, loader context, and handler primitives\r\n- `./form`: server action and form handling primitives\r\n- `./defer`: deferred server rendering and stream state utilities\r\n- `./query`: Preact Query integration and hydration helpers\r\n- `./server`: Fresh server setup, middleware, and plugin runtime\r\n- `./streams`: client-side durable event stream consumers and hook helpers\r\n- `./ai`: AI assistant endpoints, stream hooks, and tool integration\r\n- `./ai/sandbox`: client-side AI code execution sandbox runtime\r\n- `./interactive`: interactive Preact client component utilities\r\n- `./vite`: Vite development server and build plugin integration\r\n- `./error`: diagnostic error boundaries and error formatting helpers\r\n- `./desktop`: desktop window container and IPC bridge helpers\r\n- `./testing`: route loader testing and assertion harness helpers\r\n\r\nFor visual UI components and design system primitives, see `@netscript/fresh-ui`. Visual components are copied into your app (via `ui:add`), not imported from the package.\r\n\r\nRead your generated app's scaffold (`routes/` and `components/ui/mod.ts`) to see the intended app structure and usage patterns; package docs describe API symbols and types.\r\n@module\r\n\r\nDefined in file:///home/codex/repos/ns004-docs/packages/fresh/src/application/cache-entries/mod.ts:19:1\r\n\r\nfunction hasAllCacheEntries(entries: ReadonlyArray\u003cCacheEntryLike\u003cunknown\u003e | null | undefined\u003e): boolean\r\n  Return `true` when every supplied entry is present.\r\n\r\nDefined in file:///home/codex/repos/ns004-docs/packages/fresh/src/application/cache-entries/mod.ts:28:1\r\n\r\nfunction minCachedAt(entries: ReadonlyArray\u003cCacheEntryLike\u003cunknown\u003e | null | undefined\u003e): number | undefined\r\n  Return the oldest `cachedAt` timestamp across the supplied entries.\r\n\r\nDefined in file:///home/codex/repos/ns004-docs/packages/fresh/src/application/cache-entries/mod.ts:37:1\r\n\r\nfunction projectCachedItemFromList\u003cTItem\u003e(listEntry: CachedListEntryLike\u003cTItem\u003e | null | undefined, predicate: (item: TItem) =\u003e boolean): CacheEntryLike\u003cTItem\u003e | undefined\r\n  Project a single cached item from a cached list response while preserving the list timestamp.\r\n\r\nDefined in file:///home/codex/repos/ns004-docs/packages/fresh/src/application/cache-entries/cache-entry.ts:3:1\r\n\r\ninterface CacheEntryLike\u003cT\u003e\r\n  Cached-entry shape shared by page loaders and partial orchestration.\r\n\r\n  readonly data: T\r\n    Cached payload.\r\n  readonly cachedAt: number\r\n    Unix epoch timestamp in milliseconds.\r\n\r\nDefined in file:///home/codex/repos/ns004-docs/packages/fresh/src/application/cache-entries/cache-entry.ts:11:1\r\n\r\ninterface CachedListEntryLike\u003cTItem\u003e\r\n  Cached list-entry shape used when projecting a single list item.\r\n\r\n  data: { items: TItem[]; }\r\n    Cached list payload.\r\n  cachedAt: number\r\n    Unix epoch timestamp in milliseconds.\r\n\r\n"}}}
